[resource]
script = ExtResource("1_plan")
title = "Open ground, 30 seats a side"
question = "FOUR FORCE DESIGNS AT THE SAME PRICE, on the longest open run in the repo. Every side costs exactly 30 SUPPLY SEATS — infantry 1, rover and Lobber 2, walker 3 — so the question is not who brought more, it is which SHAPE of force wins for the same seats.

  MASS       30 rifles
  BALANCED   4 walkers + 5 rovers + 8 rifles
  WEDGE      8 walkers + 6 rifles
  ARTILLERY  8 Lobbers + 14 rifles

1 asks whether numbers beat combined arms. 2 is the extreme version — almost all armour against almost all bodies. 3 asks whether indirect fire pays for itself over a 200 m approach, which is the fight Lobbers are supposed to be for. 4 is the mirror control: it should come out near even, and if it does not, the map or the spawn is doing something the other three results would inherit.

Sides swap every other run. Three repeats only — sixty robots a fight is expensive — so read these as a direction, not a settled number.

Run before the armour rule lands and again after: matchup 2 in particular should change completely, since today a rifle takes the same bite out of a walker as out of a trooper."
matchups = Array[Resource]([SubResource("M1"), SubResource("M2"), SubResource("M3"), SubResource("M4")])
level = ExtResource("8_coast")
site = Vector3(0, 0, 24)
site_heading = 90.0
repeats_override = 0
speed = 4.0
